body:
I'm not sure if this is due to my own misunderstanding of how Psalm works, but I figured this was the best place to report/ask this question.

|                         |                                          |
| --------------|-------------------------|
| **Expected** | Psalm reports no errors |
| **Actual**      | Psalm reports a `MissingThrowsDocblock` error |

I set the `checkForThrowsDocblock` attribute to true in `psalm.xml` and ran the tool. It reported a few missing `@throws` annotations which I fixed. One of the methods that Psalm reports an error for doesn't throw an exception on its own, rather a method it calls throws one which then bubbles up through the call stack.

I added `@psalm-suppress MissingThrowsDocblock` annotation above the method declaration and later inline, immediately above the call that would throw an exception.

Here's the output from my command line:

```
./vendor/bin/psalm --show-info=false
Scanning files...
Analyzing files...

ERROR: MissingThrowsDocblock - src/Http/Message/Response.php:15:5 - UnexpectedValueException is thrown but not caught - please either catch or add a @throws annotation
    /**
     * @psalm-suppress MissingThrowsDocblock 
     */
    protected function build(): string {


------------------------------
1 errors found
------------------------------

Checks took 0.24 seconds and used 27.327MB of memory
Psalm was able to infer types for 95.939% of analyzed code (22 files)
```

And here's the method if that helps any:

**Response.php**
```php
/**
 * $container->getStatusMessage() may throw an UnexpectedValueException, and it has the annotation.
 * @psalm-suppress MissingThrowsDocblock
 */
protected function build(): string {
    $compiled = sprintf("%s %s %s\n",
        $this->container->getVersion(),
        $this->container->getStatusCode(),
        $this->container->getStatusMessage()
    );

    $headers = iterator_to_array($this->container->getHeaders());

    if ($headers) {
        array_walk($headers, function ($v, $k) use (&$compiled) {
            $compiled .= "{$k}: {$v}\n";
        });
    }

    $body = $this->container->getBody();

    if ($body) {
        $compiled .= "\n{$body}";
    }

    return $compiled;
}
```

**psalm.xml**
```xml
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<psalm
    totallyTyped="false"
    checkForThrowsDocblock="true"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xmlns="https://getpsalm.org/schema/config"
    xsi:schemaLocation="https://getpsalm.org/schema/config file:///Users/pbice/dev/9933-consulting/vendor/vimeo/psalm/config.xsd"
>
```

What am I doing wrong? Or is this an issue with Psalm?
